    "learnings": {
      "repo": [
        "apps/web/src/wasm/cipherbox_wasm.d.ts (checked-in wasm bindings) is a gitignored build artifact, so stale doc comments there don't need fixing manually.",
        "ReceivedVerdict.permission can only rise via the ResolutionClass::Granted arm reading committed_permission from an owner-signed commitment at the recipient-blinded tag (received_status.rs:401-408); no other verdict class (Unresolvable, EpochLag, RevocationSignal, Cut) can raise permission.",
        "The write capability is gated separately from the display permission: writable_graft_roots (facade.rs:11354-11365) and snapshot permission (facade.rs:10410-10419) both check bookmarked_permissions plus an in-memory write seed, so the row's displayed permission is never itself a capability.",
        "accept.rs:282 writable_scope_refs still reads the superseded bookmark copy of permission rather than the live verdict, but currently has no production caller so it's a latent (not active) gap."
      ],
      "code": [
        {
          "path": "crates/engine/src/grants/received_status.rs",
          "line": 96,
          "end_line": 101,
          "finding": "New live_permission helper is an exact extraction of the closure refresh already used to build render.permissions; call site (462-464) preserves identical values."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/engine/src/facade.rs",
          "line": 10581,
          "finding": "received_shares() row read switched from share.permission (stale bookmark) to live_permission, closing a display/gate divergence."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/engine/src/grants/accept.rs",
          "line": 282,
          "finding": "writable_scope_refs() still filters on the bookmark's superseded permission field; safe today only because no caller exists yet — must be updated to use live_permission when a caller is added."
        }
      ],
      "workflow": [
        "Running a security-review gate and a domain-specific crypto-privacy review gate in parallel as background subagents for a sensitive PR before requesting human reviewers.",
        "Checking whether a flagged file is a tracked/build artifact before deciding to act on a review finding (avoids wasted fix for gitignored generated files).",
        "Checking CodeRabbit's last review timestamp before pushing to avoid burning/colliding with its review slot."
      ]
